{
 "artist": "Claude Monet",
 "slug": "claude-monet",
 "born": 1840,
 "died": 1926,
 "nationality": "French",
 "facts": [
  {
   "text": "Monet signed with his full name, 'Claude Monet', from the 1860s to the 1900s, usually adding a two-digit year in the 1870s–1890s and the full year in the 1900s.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.46657.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "He did not always sign when he painted: on Boats on the Beach at Étretat (1885) the signature was added after the picture had already been varnished.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/digital-publications/48/monet-paintings-and-drawings-at-the-art-institute-of-chicago-2/392/cats-22-23-etretat-1885",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  },
  {
   "text": "A signed date is not always the year of painting: The Artist's Garden at Vétheuil, painted in 1881, is signed 'Claude Monet 80'.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.52189.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many late canvases were never signed; when they left the studio after his death they were given a stamped 'Claude Monet' signature, which the Art Institute of Chicago notes does not quite match his own handwriting.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/digital-publications/48/monet-paintings-and-drawings-at-the-art-institute-of-chicago-2/420/cat-46-irises-191417",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  },
  {
   "text": "The estate stamps were probably applied by his son Michel, who inherited the studio, likely with the Paris dealer Katia Granoff, who sold many of the late works.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/digital-publications/48/monet-paintings-and-drawings-at-the-art-institute-of-chicago-2/420/cat-46-irises-191417",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  }
 ],
